Key definitions and formulas
- CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost) = Total sales & marketing spend in a period / Number of new customers acquired in that period
- ARPU (average revenue per user) typically = Revenue in period / number of customers (express as monthly or annual)
- Gross margin contribution per customer (monthly) = ARPU_monthly * gross_margin%
- Churn rate (periodic, typically annual for SaaS): proportion of customers lost per year
- LTV (for subscription/SaaS) = (ARPU_annual * gross_margin) / churn_rate
  - Equivalent monthly formula: LTV = (ARPU_monthly * gross_margin) / monthly_churn
- CAC payback (months) = CAC / (monthly gross margin per customer)
- Healthy benchmark targets: LTV:CAC >= 3x, CAC payback <= 12 months (target depends on stage)

