A. Key formulas and what I need from you
- CAC (customer acquisition cost) = Total Sales & Marketing spend in a period / Number of new customers acquired in that period.
  - Inputs needed: S&M spend (quarterly or monthly) and # of new customers acquired in that same period.
- ARPU (average revenue per user) = Total revenue in period / Average number of customers during that period.
  - Inputs needed: revenue and customer counts (or MRR per customer).
- Gross margin per customer = ARPU * gross margin % (where gross margin % = (revenue − COGS)/revenue).
  - Input needed: gross margin % (or COGS).
- Customer lifetime (in months) = 1 / monthly churn rate (for subscription models). For non-subscription, use average repeat purchases or lifespan.
  - Input needed: monthly churn rate (or annual churn).
- LTV (Customer Lifetime Value) = ARPU * gross margin % * (1 / monthly churn rate)  (if you use monthly metrics)
  - Alternative LTV (simpler): LTV = ARPU * average customer lifetime (in months) * gross margin %
- LTV : CAC ratio — target benchmark typically >= 3:1.
- Payback period (months) = CAC / (ARPU * gross margin %). Target often < 12 months for growth-stage companies.

B. Illustrative scenarios (useful to show stakeholders how changes move the needle)
Context you gave: cash $2.1M, burn $240K/month (20 months runway), revenue last quarter $3.2M → monthly revenue ≈ $1.067M.

I’ll show three sample scenarios (these are illustrative — I’ll recalc with your real S&M spend, new customers, churn, margin if you provide them).

Assumptions common to all examples:
- Monthly revenue = $1,067,000
- Assume average ARPU (monthly revenue / number of customers) — I’ll pick customer counts to illustrate.

Scenario A — Base case
- Avg customers ≈ 1,067 (so ARPU ≈ $1,000/month)
- Quarterly S&M spend = 30% of revenue = $960K (example)
- New customers that quarter = 300
- Quarterly S&M spend converts to CAC = 960,000 / 300 = $3,200 per new customer
- Gross margin = 70%
- Monthly churn = 3% → average lifetime ≈ 33 months
- LTV = ARPU * gross margin / churn = 1,000 * 0.7 / 0.03 ≈ $23,333
- LTV:CAC ≈ 23,333 / 3,200 ≈ 7.3 : 1 (very healthy)
- Payback period = CAC / (ARPU * gross margin) = 3,200 / 700 ≈ 4.6 months

Scenario B — Conservative
- Same ARPU $1,000/month
- Quarterly S&M spend = 40% of revenue = $1.28M
- New customers = 300 (less efficient)
- CAC = 1,280,000 / 300 ≈ $4,267
