Required inputs
- Sales & marketing spend for the period you want to measure (monthly or quarterly).
- Number of new customers acquired in that same period (or total customers at start and end to infer new adds).
- Average revenue per customer (ARPU) for the same period (monthly or annual) OR number of customers + total revenue so I can compute ARPU.
- Gross margin (contribution margin %) on revenue (for SaaS this is typically 60–90%; for product businesses different).
- Customer churn (monthly or annual) or average customer lifetime.

If you provide those I’ll calculate exact CAC, LTV, payback, and LTV/CAC.

Key formulas (what I’ll use)
- CAC = Total Sales & Marketing Spend (period) / Number of New Customers (same period).
- ARPU (monthly) = Total Revenue (month) / # customers (month). (Or derive from ACV/ARR.)
- Customer lifetime (in months) ≈ 1 / monthly churn_rate (if churn is roughly constant).
- LTV (gross-margin based) = ARPU_monthly × Gross_Margin% × Customer_lifetime_months.
- Payback months = CAC / (ARPU_monthly × Gross_Margin%).
- LTV / CAC ratio = LTV / CAC.
- For NPV LTV, discount future gross profits (I can do that if you want a 10%/year or other discount).

Quick context using your existing numbers
- Revenue last quarter = $3.2M → monthly revenue ≈ $1.067M; annualized run-rate ≈ $12.8M.
